            <ArticleTitle>Etomidate in a new solvent. A clinical evaluation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>996-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The introduction of polyethylene glycol as a solvent for etomidate appears to markedly reduce the incidence of pain on injection while maintaining the previously demonstrated advantageous features of cardiovascular stability and rapid recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
